<title>ITALY: NORDIC SKIING-RESULTS FROM WORLD CUP COMBINED EVENT.</title>
<headline>NORDIC SKIING-RESULTS FROM WORLD CUP COMBINED EVENT.</headline>
<dateline>PREDAZZO, Italy 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results of the</p>
<p>floodlit ski jumping leg of a Nordic skiing combined World Cup</p>
<p>event on Tuesday</p>
<p>1. Michael Gruber (Austria) 240.0 points (first jump 93.0</p>
<p>metres/second jump 90.5 metres)</p>
<p>2. Andrea Longo (Italy) 239.0 (95.0/88.0)</p>
<p>3. Samppa Lajunen (Finland) 237.5 (95.5/88.0)</p>
<p>4. Christoph Bieler (Austria) 234.0 (90.5/91.0)</p>
<p>5. Jari Mantila (Finland) 230.0 (87.5/92.0)</p>
<p>6. Ludovic Roux (France) 229.5 (90.5/89.0)</p>
<p>7. Kristian Hammer (Norway) 228.0 (90.0/89.0)</p>
<p>8. Toni Kilponen (Finland) 225.0 (89.5/87.5)</p>
<p>9. Mario Stecher (Austria) 223.0 (86.0/91.0)</p>
<p>10 equal. Alexej Barannikov (Russia) 217.0 (87.0/88.0)</p>
<p>10 equal. Walerij Stoljarov (Russia) 217.0 (89.0/85.0)</p>
<p>(Second part of event takes place on Wednesday).</p>
</text>
